Well, here is the obligatory ascention post.

This is my second win, but only my first brag post.  I didn't brag the
first time because I used cheats (spoilers) and I was a Barbarian --
which is the easiest race, as far as I'm concerned.  For the curious,
I saved a name.sav file and played it again when I died.  This is an
obvious cheat, so I count this time as my first real victory.  

This time I was a wizard though, so I feel I have the right to brag.
Pretty basic character and a pretty quick game.  Didn't polypile,
didn't generate gold, didn't cheat AT ALL.  So there!

I reached experience level 14, 123 hp., 57 pw., AC -31 (Good, eh?)
I was helped by finding a ghost level on 16 containing a +3 GDSC,
a +3 cloak of displacement, and about 30,000 in gold (hence the -31 AC).

The main problem I had was not having a ring of levitation.  I had to
trek all the way down to level 1 and back from the castle (level 28) and
finally got one through a water demon wish.  Also, I didn't get any wishes
except that one until the castle.  I really didn't need them, but they
sure are fun.

I was aided by the following:
Blessed amulet of life saving (never used)- from a wish
Blessed +7 Excalibur- made it myself!
Gauntlets of Power- just found them.  Had a 18/20 by the end anyway.
Blessed speed boots- another wish
Blessed +2 shield of reflection- wish.
+3 GDSC- bones score.
Blessed +4 cloak of displacement- bones again.
Blessed +2 helm of telepathy- wish (great item!)
+4 ring of protection- from a barracks.  Not really necessary.
Ring of conflict (started with it- makes for a much easier game!)
Luckstone (Had ~8 or 9 luck.)

Intrinsics:
Teleportation (F.E.)
See invisible - Stalker corpse.
Poison resistance - don't recall how I got it...?
Fire res. (red mold)
Cold res. - don't recall.  I think from an ice troll.
Cause conflict (Da ring)
Protection (ring)
Teleport control (tengu man)
Fast (speed boots, Q corpse first)
Invisible to others (blessed potion of Invis.) * My favorite potion
Reflection (shield - never really needed it though)
Life will be saved - from the amulet
Mag. protected - Everyone's favorite suit of mail.  Saved my ass.
Displaced - Another of my favorites
Extra luck - many corpses up in smoke
Good/bad luck does not time out - the luckstone.
Telepathic - from our good friend the Eye.

Missing: Stealth - one of my favorite intrinsics.
         Sleep resistance - I tried real hard but never got it.

My vote for the most crucial object in the game:

A ring of Levitation.

And not just because I couldn't find one.  It's one of the essential
things to solve the game.  I suppose water-walking boots would help, but
the ring is so much easier.  In addition, you also need fireproofness,
which I got early somehow.  I usually do not use conflict, as I prefer to
have invisibility, displacement, and stealth all at once.  As far
as the enemy is concerned, you don't even exist with these three things.
Conflict may be a cheap win but it's a win nonetheless.

I also genocided some toughies- L's, D's, and T's.  But not before a Lich
cursed my gauntlets of power.  It's a damn good thing he did too, because
I was wielding a cocatrice corpse while trying to put on a new ring.
For those who don't know, this is a real boo-boo while wielding that
little "c."  Almost pulled the ultimate bonehead move.

All told, I had a whopping 761,888 points in 26,461 moves.  I could have
had many more points if I'd kept any gems.  I donated all of my gold to
Thoth for the AC too.  I could have had far fewer moves had I been able
to locate a ring of levitation.  But who plays for points?

I think the Wizard is probably the hardest character to ascend with.
You've really gotta play it safe in combat.  But then when you get to
the end, it sure feels nice to wipe out Giants in two swipes.  I also
used very very few spells.  Maybe 5 or 6 times the whole game, and I
knew about 10 spells.  I hope they devise a new magic system in the
next version. 

Whew!  Wizard and Barbarians down.  Next comes the Priest!

